# CHAPTER I

## GENERAL PROVISIONS

#### Article 1

In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:

1. Region is South Bangka Regency.  
2. Regional Government is the administration of governmental affairs by the regional government and the Regional House of Representatives according to the principles of autonomy and assistance tasks with the principle of the widest possible autonomy within the system and principles of the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia as referred to in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia.  
3. Regional Government is the Regent as an element of the Regional Government administrator who leads the implementation of governmental affairs that are the authority of the autonomous region.  
4. Regent is the Regent of South Bangka.  
5. Regional House of Representatives hereinafter abbreviated as DPRD is the Regional House of Representatives of South Bangka Regency.  
6. Human Rights are a set of rights inherent in the nature and existence of human beings as creatures of God Almighty and are His gifts that must be respected, upheld and protected by the state, law, government, and every person for the sake of honor and protection of human dignity and worth.  
7. Women's empowerment is every effort to improve physical, mental spiritual, social capacity, knowledge and skills so that women are ready to be utilized according to their respective abilities.  
8. Women's protection is all efforts aimed at providing a sense of security to women carried out by family, advocates, social institutions, police, prosecutors, courts or other parties either temporarily or based on court decisions.  
9. Discrimination is any restriction, harassment or exclusion that is directly or indirectly based on human differentiation on the basis of religion, ethnicity, race, ethnic group, group, class, social status, economic status, gender, language, political beliefs, which results in the reduction, deviation or elimination of recognition, implementation or use of human rights and fundamental freedoms in life both individually and collectively in the political, economic, legal, social, cultural and other aspects of life.  
10. Gender is a concept that refers to roles and responsibilities as women and as men that are created and internalized in families, society and the culture of the society in which we live including expectations, attitudes, characteristics, behavior of how to be a man and how to be a woman.  
11. Gender Equality is the equality of conditions for men and women to obtain opportunities and their rights as human beings to be able to play a role and participate in political, economic, socio-cultural, defense and security activities, and equality in enjoying the results of development.  
12. Violence against women is any act that violates, hinders, eliminates the enjoyment and disregards the human rights of women.  
13. Disability is an individual who has physical or mental limitations.  
14. Society is individuals, families, groups and social organizations and/or community organizations. 15. Family is the smallest unit in society consisting of husband and wife, husband-wife and their children, or father and his children, or mother and her children.  
16. Labor is every person who is capable of doing work to produce goods and/or services either to meet their own needs or for society.  
17. Worker/laborer is every person who works by receiving wages or remuneration in other forms.

# CHAPTER II

## SCOPE

#### Article 2

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:  
a. Principles and objectives;  
b. Women's rights;  
c. Obligations and Responsibilities of the Regional Government;  
d. Women's Empowerment;  
e. Women's Protection;  
f. Strategy for Women's Empowerment and Protection;  
g. Mechanism for Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Protection;  
h. Community Participation;  
i. Funding; and  
j. Guidance and Supervision.  

www.jdih.bangkaselatankab.go.id

# CHAPTER III

## PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

#### Article 3

Women's Empowerment and Protection is implemented based on the principles of:  
a. respect for human rights;  
b. justice and gender equality;  
c. non-discrimination; and  
d. victim protection.

#### Article 4

Women's Empowerment and Protection aims to:  
a. increase women's participation in the development process;  
b. improve the quality of life of women;  
c. provide guarantees to women in the fulfillment of rights as human beings; and. 
d. provide a sense of security by increasing protection for women from various acts of violence.

# CHAPTER IV

## WOMEN'S RIGHTS

#### Article 5

1. Every woman has the right to:  
a. live and maintain life and improve her standard of living;  
b. fulfill her basic needs to grow and develop properly, have a family and continue offspring;  
c. develop her personality, to obtain education, and improve her quality of life to become a human being who is faithful, pious, responsible, noble, happy, and prosperous in accordance with human rights;  
d. obtain justice, security, and freedom to express opinions without discrimination;  
e. be involved in every stage of the development process;  
f. be free from slavery or enslavement and threats;  
g. obtain protection of her person, family, honor, dignity and property rights;  
h. obtain welfare and a decent life;  
i. participate in politics;  
j. perform legal acts; and  
k. freely choose a partner in her marriage.
2. Every wife during the marriage bond has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband over all matters relating to her married life, relations with her children, and ownership and management of joint property in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.  
3. After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has rights and responsibilities with her former husband over all matters relating to children with due regard to the best interests of the child.

# CHAPTER V

## OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF THE REGIONAL GOVERNMENT

#### Article 6

1. The Regional Government is obligated and responsible for the empowerment and protection of women.  
2. Efforts for the empowerment and protection of women as referred to in paragraph (1), include:  
a. determination of policies, programs, and activities;  
b. determination of implementation guidelines;  
c. provision of services; and  
d. coordination of policies, programs and activities.  
3. Efforts for the empowerment and protection of women as referred to in paragraph (2) are carried out in an integrated manner in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.

# CHAPTER VI

## WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT

#### Article 7

Women's empowerment is directed to obtain opportunities and rights as human beings to be able to play a role and participate in the fields of:  
a. economy;  
b. socio-culture;  
c. politics and government;  
d. law;  
e. education;  
f. health;  
g. employment; and  
h. social security.

## Part One

Economic Field

#### Article 8

Women's empowerment in the economic field is implemented through:  
a. provision of skills and job training;  
b. facilitation of the formation of productive economic business groups;  
c. facilitation of strengthening and development of productive economic business groups;  
d. facilitation and capital assistance; and  
e. facilitation of marketing network development.

## Part Two

Socio-Cultural Field
